---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Terms & Conditions — Soci Pizza">
  <section class="t bg-cream">
    <div class="t-col">
      <h1><strong>Terms &amp; Conditions</strong></h1>
      <h4>A few details to keep your pizza event running smoothly.</h4>
      <div class="t-body">
<p><strong>Deposit &amp; Reschedule Policy</strong></p>
<p>All deposits are non-refundable, as they secure your event date and allow us to turn away other booking requests.</p>
<p>One reschedule per booking is permitted, subject to calendar availability. Requests made at least 7 days before the event qualify for a deposit transfer to the new date. Requests made within 7 days of the event will be considered on a case by case basis.</p>
<p>If a last minute reschedule results in unrecoverable costs for staffing, ingredients, or other event related expenses, those costs must be settled separately before the new date is confirmed.</p>
<p><strong>Weather Policy</strong></p>
<p>Soci Pizza operates outdoors and will make every reasonable effort to complete service in light rain or typical conditions with appropriate coverings. However, in cases of severe weather, including heavy rain, high winds, or other unsafe or inoperable conditions, we reserve the right to pause, modify, or discontinue service for safety reasons.</p>
<p>If service cannot proceed due to weather, we will work with you to reschedule (subject to availability).</p>
<p>Even when our truck and/or tent is used, we strongly recommend having a backup covered area available that can accommodate at least two 6-foot tables and allow for safe operation of propane-based pizza ovens and related equipment.</p>
<p><strong>Service Conditions</strong></p>
<p>Client is responsible for providing a safe, accessible, and level setup area for equipment and service. For our Truck Package, Client is also responsible for ensuring safe vehicle access to and from the event location, including a minimum of 14 feet of overhead clearance, adequate road width and turning space, and access free of low-hanging branches or other obstructions. Access routes must have suitable ground conditions to support the vehicle.</p>
<p>We reserve the right to adjust or decline setup if conditions are unsafe, including but not limited to unstable ground, excessive wind exposure, restricted space, or unsuitable vehicle access.</p>
<p>Service timing, output, and flow may vary depending on conditions, guest count, and environment. While we aim to serve efficiently, exact production rates are not guaranteed.</p>
<p><strong>Venue Requirements &amp; Additional Services</strong></p>
<p>Clients are responsible for confirming that their venue permits Soci Pizza's services, including any required food trucks, tents, equipment, and outdoor cooking.</p>
<p>Our services are limited to those outlined in the selected package and on our website. Any additional venue requirements or requests outside our standard services, such as guest trash collection or additional cleanup, must be discussed and approved in advance and may incur additional charges.</p>
<p><strong>Event Confirmation &amp; Client Responsibility</strong></p>
<p>It is the client’s responsibility to review and confirm all event details (including date, time, location, guest count, and service requirements) prior to the event. Any corrections or discrepancies must be communicated in writing prior to service.</p>
<p>The most recent written invoice or event summary issued by Soci Pizza supersedes prior communications regarding event details unless otherwise confirmed in writing by Soci Pizza.</p>
<p>Silence or lack of response to an invoice or event summary does not constitute confirmation.</p>
<p>The client is responsible for ensuring that all relevant parties (including planners, coordinators, venues, and other vendors) are aligned with final event details. Soci Pizza is not responsible for miscommunication between third parties involved in event coordination.</p>
<p>A booking is not considered fully confirmed until Soci Pizza issues a final invoice. It is the client’s responsibility to review this invoice and communicate any corrections in writing. If no written corrections are received, the details will be considered accepted.</p>
<p><strong>Limitation of Liability</strong></p>
<p>In all cases, Soci Pizza’s liability is limited to the amount paid for the booking deposit. Soci Pizza is not liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential damages, including but not limited to coordination issues or third-party planning or communication errors.</p>
<p><strong>Safety &amp; Liability</strong></p>
<p>Our setup includes high-temperature cooking equipment. For safety, guests must maintain a reasonable distance from cooking and prep areas. Soci Pizza is not liable for injuries or damages resulting from unsafe guest behavior or interference with equipment.</p>
<p><strong>Delays &amp; Unforeseen Circumstances</strong></p>
<p>Soci Pizza is not responsible for delays or inability to perform due to circumstances beyond our control, including but not limited to severe weather, road closures, accidents causing major traffic disruption, venue access restrictions, or emergencies.</p>
<p><strong>Terms Updates</strong></p>
<p>Soci Pizza reserves the right to update or modify these Terms &amp; Conditions at any time.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .t { padding: 70px 0 8vw; }
  .t-col { width: 45.6vw; margin-left: 27.25vw; }
  .t h1 { margin-bottom: 0.4em; }
  .t h4 { margin-bottom: 1.4em; }
  .t-body p { font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .t-body p:has(> strong:only-child) { font-size: var(--fs-body); margin-top: 28px; }
  @media (max-width: 767px) { .t-col { width: auto; margin: 0 24px; } }
</style>
